      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Greek yogurt and deli turkey are great additions to your protein-rich diet, as they're generally considered safe with MAOIs. However, be cautious with fermented foods like kombucha and pickles, as some of them can contain higher levels of tyramine than others. Examples of fermented foods to limit or avoid might include cheese-producing bacteria, aged cheeses, miso, fish sauce, or pickled herring; it's always best to consult your doctor for personalized guidance.",
